============================================================
        DEEPSEEK LOCAL CODING AGENT — PROJECT ROADMAP
============================================================

FINAL GOAL
------------------------------------------------------------
Build a locally running, Claude Code-style coding agent powered
by DeepSeek through Ollama.

The agent should be able to:

  Understand an unfamiliar Git repository
  Read and search files
  Plan coding tasks
  Create / edit / delete files with approval
  Run commands and tests
  Review its own changes
  Save DeepSeek reasoning traces in .reason files
  Inspect Git status and diffs
  Commit approved changes
  Push approved changes to GitHub


PHASE SUMMARY
------------------------------------------------------------

FOUNDATION
  Phase 0  → Final Architecture
  Phase 1  → Environment & Hardware Validation
  Phase 2  → Ollama / DeepSeek Model Layer
  Phase 3  → Agent Runtime
  Phase 4  → Repository Discovery
  Phase 5  → Tool System
  Phase 6  → File Reading
  Phase 7  → Repository Search

MVP — THE CORE CODING AGENT
  Phase 8  → File Editing
  Phase 9  → Command Execution
  Phase 10 → Safety & Approval System
  Phase 11 → Git Integration
  Phase 12 → Self-Review & Testing Loop
  Phase 13 → Git Commit
  Phase 14 → Git Push

V1 — RELIABLE & SCALABLE AGENT
  Phase 15 → Context Management
  Phase 16 → Large Repository Support
  Phase 17 → Failure Recovery
  Phase 18 → Project Instructions
  Phase 19 → Session Management
  Phase 20 → Evaluation Framework
  Phase 21 → Performance Optimization
  Phase 22 → Model Benchmarking

V2 — ADVANCED GITHUB WORKFLOWS
  Phase 23 → GitHub API Integration
  Phase 24 → Issue & Pull Request Automation


